---
import AboutHeroImage from '../assets/blog-placeholder-about.jpg';
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../consts';
---

<Layout
	title="About Me"
	description="Vorrapong Kertnat (ICE) — full-stack developer at BAAC in Bangkok, currently studying Financial Engineering at UTCC."
	pubDate={new Date('August 18 2026')}
	heroImage={AboutHeroImage}
>
	<p>
		สวัสดีครับ — I'm <strong>Vorrapong Kertnat</strong>, everyone calls me <strong style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#67e8f9,#a78bfa 35%,#f9a8d4);-webkit-background-clip:text;background-clip:text;color:#0000;letter-spacing:.08em;font-weight:800">ICE</strong>
	</p>

	<p>
		I'm a full-stack developer at the <strong
			>Bank for Agriculture and Agricultural Cooperatives (BAAC)</strong
		> in Bangkok. I studied Computer Engineering at Prince of Songkla University, graduated in 2021,
		and have been building software professionally ever since — mostly TypeScript, mostly on systems
		that real people depend on.
	</p>

	<h2>What I'm into right now</h2>

	<p>
		In June 2026 I started a master's in <strong>Financial Engineering</strong> at the UTCC Graduate
		School, and it has quietly taken over my side projects. My GitHub has drifted away from web APIs
		and toward portfolio analytics, risk models, and QuantLib experiments. It turns out that after a
		few years of building banking systems, I wanted to understand the math running underneath them.
	</p>

	<p>
		By day I'm on the Office Automation System (OAS) team at BAAC, working mostly in Vue and
		ElysiaJS. By night it's coursework, portfolio math, and the occasional video game.
	</p>

	<h2>What I build with</h2>

	<p>
		TypeScript is my daily driver. On the backend I reach for <strong>ElysiaJS</strong> — I like it
		enough that I've contributed to its documentation — along with NestJS and Express. On the front
		end, React and Vue. For data: PostgreSQL, MongoDB, SQL Server, and Oracle.
	</p>

	<p>
		A good chunk of my job is DevSecOps, so I spend a lot of time with Docker, Kubernetes,
		OpenShift, ArgoCD, Helm, Jenkins, SonarQube, Trivy, and Ansible. On the side I've been learning
		<strong>Rust</strong> — slowly, and stubbornly.
	</p>

	<h2>Where I've been</h2>

	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>BAAC</strong> — Full Stack Developer, Feb 2024 – present
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>AIS</strong> — Senior Programmer Analyst, Sep 2023 – Jan 2024
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Sirisoft</strong> — Software Developer, Dec 2021 – Sep 2023
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Prince of Songkla University</strong> — Teaching Assistant for Basic Engineering Programming
			(Python), Jun – Sep 2021
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>NextHop</strong> — Back-end Developer Intern (Express, MongoDB), Apr – Jun 2021
		</li>
	</ul>

	<p>
		Along the way I've picked up a pile of certifications — Kubernetes for Developers (LFD259), Red
		Hat OpenShift Virtualization, GitOps Fundamentals, Docker Foundations, a stack of Microsoft
		Azure fundamentals, and most recently Prompt Engineering &amp; Agentic AI. They're all on <a href="https://www.credly.com/users/vorrapong-kertnat/badges" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
			>my Credly profile</a
		> if you're curious.
	</p>

	<h2>Writing</h2>

	<p>
		I write on <a href="https://medium.com/@iceman951" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Medium</a
		>, mostly in Thai and mostly about ElysiaJS — using TypeORM's QueryRunner to handle
		transactions, or wiring up a health-check service with cron jobs and Nodemailer. Generally I
		write up whatever I just had to figure out the hard way, so I don't have to figure it out twice.
	</p>

	<h2>Away from the keyboard</h2>

	<p>
		I shoot competitively — or at least I used to. I was a student athlete and later a committee
		member of the Prince of Songkla University Shooting Club from 2017 to 2020. I also play guitar;
		my very first published article wasn't about code at all, it was about which bass string to play
		for a given chord. I follow football closely enough that two of my side projects are player
		injury trackers. And yes, there was a phase in 2021–2022 involving GPU mining and blockchain
		write-ups. Every developer gets one crypto phase.
	</p>

	<h2>Find me</h2>

	<ul>
		<li>
			Email — <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
		</li>
		<li>
			GitHub — <a href="https://github.com/iceman951" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
				>@iceman951</a
			>
		</li>
		<li>
			LinkedIn — <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/vorrapong/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
				>in/vorrapong</a
			>
		</li>
		<li>
			Medium — <a href="https://medium.com/@iceman951" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
				>@iceman951</a
			>
		</li>
	</ul>

</Layout>
